From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/linlondp: pin display power domain unconditionally

With the SCMI POWER genpd now live (patches-7.2/0132), the display DPU
power domain is a genuinely gated genpd domain rather than an
always-on rail. The KMS master bind only pinned the domain active when
the driver inherited the UEFI GOP framebuffer (mdevs[0]->enabled_by_gop).

When Linux does NOT inherit a GOP framebuffer (headless bring-up, or a
mode the firmware did not light), nothing holds a runtime-PM reference
on the display domain, so genpd_power_off_unused() powers it off during
late init. The DP transmitter then reads HPD as 0, the connector is
reported disconnected, and the modeset fails with "Cannot find any crtc
or sizes" -> permanent blank screen.

Hold an unconditional runtime-PM reference on every DPU in the cluster
so the display power domain stays powered through modeset and detect,
and release it in unbind. This is the same net effect the GOP path had,
applied to every DPU regardless of GOP inheritance.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream ACPI/PM enablement for CIX Sky1]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c
index 28381b9..dcc338c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/linlon-dp/linlondp_cluster.c
@@ -112,7 +112,6 @@ static bool linlondp_cluster_is_direct_mdev(struct device *dev,
 static int linlondp_cluster_bind(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct linlondp_cluster *cl = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-	struct device *d0 = cl->mdevs[0]->dev;
 	unsigned int i;
 	int err;
 
@@ -157,8 +156,20 @@ static int linlondp_cluster_bind(struct device *dev)
 	if (enable_fb)
 		drm_client_setup(&cl->kms->base, NULL);
 
-	if (cl->mdevs[0]->enabled_by_gop)
-		pm_runtime_set_active(d0);
+	/*
+	 * SCMI POWER genpd is now live (patches-7.2/0132) so the display
+	 * power domain is genuinely gated; previously it was only pinned
+	 * when the UEFI GOP framebuffer was inherited (enabled_by_gop).
+	 * Without GOP, genpd_power_off_unused() powers the display domain
+	 * off -> DPTX HPD reads 0 -> connector reported disconnected ->
+	 * "Cannot find any crtc or sizes" -> blank screen.  Hold an
+	 * unconditional runtime-PM ref on every DPU so the domain stays
+	 * powered through modeset and detect.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < cl->n_mdevs; i++) {
+		pm_runtime_set_active(cl->mdevs[i]->dev);
+		pm_runtime_get_noresume(cl->mdevs[i]->dev);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -179,6 +190,8 @@ static void linlondp_cluster_unbind(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < cl->n_mdevs; i++) {
+		/* release the unconditional ref taken in bind */
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(cl->mdevs[i]->dev);
 		if (pm_runtime_enabled(cl->mdevs[i]->dev))
 			pm_runtime_disable(cl->mdevs[i]->dev);
 	}
